- action(n1, "start"): Hallucinates a preliminary step; the description ("To start, you need to enter your credit card number") identifies entering the credit card number as the first actual behavior, not a distinct "start" task.
- action(n4, "end procedure"): Hallucinates a concluding task; the description ("the process will come to an end") specifies immediate termination after the verification number, not an additional action node.
- precedence(i1, n1), precedence(n1, n2), precedence(n3, n4), precedence(n4, e1): Fails to preserve exact source chronology (SMC3) and intended progression (SMC5) by routing through hallucinated nodes; the control flow should directly connect init(i1) → action(n2) → action(n3) → end(e1).